{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-js","path":"/blog/2010-02-02-anonymous-delegates-and-event-execution/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p>A nice little trick to save you always checking for null when firing custom events.<br>\nInitialize to anonymous delegate.<br>\nOk... we've an extra call in the invocation list so use judiciously.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"csharp\"><pre style=\"counter-reset: linenumber NaN\" class=\"language-csharp line-numbers\"><code class=\"language-csharp\"><span class=\"token keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">event</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">CompleteTaskExecutionHandler</span> CompleteExecution <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">delegate</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token comment\">//or a sample using Lambdas</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">event</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">PropertyChangedEventHandler</span> PropertyChanged <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>s<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>p<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n\n\n\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">private</span> <span class=\"token return-type class-name\"><span class=\"token keyword\">void</span></span> <span class=\"token function\">Fire</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n   <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">CompleteExecution</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token range operator\">..</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"line-numbers-rows\" style=\"white-space: normal; width: auto; left: 0;\"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></pre></div>","timeToRead":1,"excerpt":"A nice little trick to save you always checking for null when firing custom events. Initialize to anonymous delegate. Ok... we've an extra call in the invocation list so use judiciously.","frontmatter":{"title":"Anonymous delegates and event execution","date":"02 February 2010","category":".NET & C#","tags":["delegates","events"],"image":null}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/blog/2010-02-02-anonymous-delegates-and-event-execution/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["764694655"],"slicesMap":{}}